{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And Onan knew.</b> He thought, as in 'the knowing we shall know' — an expression of entering, ikud in the vernacular." "<b>For not to him would the seed be, etc.</b> He said in his heart: if I come to my brother's wife, I destroy my land, for I will not find anyone to plow it or sow it." "<b>So as not to give seed to his brother.</b> He did not wish to give the seed of the field to his brother, for he did not wish to destroy his inheritance. As we find in the case of Ruth: 'And the redeemer said, I cannot redeem, lest I destroy my inheritance.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:07:51.145328220Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}